
---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Strength Training | Silken Valley Lifestyle"
  description="Explore strength training fundamentals, upper-body and lower-body exercises, core workouts, resistance bands, and free weights."
  heroTitle="Strength Training"
  heroText="Build strength, improve stability, and develop a balanced approach to fitness."
  heroCompact={true}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Fitness & Active Living</p>
    <h1>Strength, Stability & Conditioning</h1>
    <p>
      Strength training is an important part of maintaining
      an active and balanced lifestyle. Through resistance
      exercises, bodyweight movements, and carefully planned
      routines, you can develop muscular strength, improve
      stability, and support everyday movement.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="strength-intro">
    <h2>The Benefits of Strength Training</h2>
    <p>
      Regular strength training helps develop muscle strength,
      supports bone health, improves balance, and makes everyday
      activities easier. A well-rounded routine works different
      muscle groups while allowing sufficient time for rest
      and recovery.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="strength-grid">
    <article class="strength-card">
      <span class="strength-number">01</span>
      <h2>Strength Training Fundamentals</h2>
      <p>
        Begin with the foundations of resistance training.
        Focus on controlled movements, proper technique,
        and choosing an appropriate level of resistance.
      </p>
      <h3>Getting Started</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Begin with manageable resistance.</li>
        <li>Learn correct movement patterns.</li>
        <li>Use controlled, steady repetitions.</li>
        <li>Allow muscles time to recover.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="strength-card">
      <span class="strength-number">02</span>
      <h2>Upper-Body Strength</h2>
      <p>
        Upper-body exercises develop the muscles of the
        shoulders, chest, arms, and back. These movements
        support posture, lifting, carrying, and everyday tasks.
      </p>
      <h3>Exercises to Explore</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Wall or modified push-ups.</li>
        <li>Dumbbell shoulder presses.</li>
        <li>Seated resistance-band rows.</li>
        <li>Bicep curls and tricep extensions.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="strength-card">
      <span class="strength-number">03</span>
      <h2>Lower-Body Strength</h2>
      <p>
        Lower-body exercises strengthen the legs, hips,
        and glutes. Developing these muscles supports
        walking, climbing stairs, balance, and mobility.
      </p>
      <h3>Exercises to Explore</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Bodyweight squats or chair squats.</li>
        <li>Glute bridges.</li>
        <li>Supported reverse lunges.</li>
        <li>Standing calf raises.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="strength-card">
      <span class="strength-number">04</span>
      <h2>Core Strengthening</h2>
      <p>
        Core training works the muscles around the abdomen,
        lower back, and pelvis. A stronger core supports
        stability, posture, and controlled movement.
      </p>
      <h3>Exercises to Explore</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Bird-dog exercises.</li>
        <li>Modified planks.</li>
        <li>Dead bug exercises.</li>
        <li>Standing abdominal bracing.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="strength-card">
      <span class="strength-number">05</span>
      <h2>Resistance Bands & Free Weights</h2>
      <p>
        Resistance bands and free weights offer flexible
        ways to develop strength. They can be incorporated
        into home workouts or a more structured fitness routine.
      </p>
      <h3>Equipment to Explore</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Light and medium resistance bands.</li>
        <li>Adjustable or fixed dumbbells.</li>
        <li>Exercise mats.</li>
        <li>Stable exercise benches or chairs.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="strength-card">
      <span class="strength-number">06</span>
      <h2>Functional Strength</h2>
      <p>
        Functional exercises develop strength for everyday
        activities such as standing, reaching, lifting,
        carrying, and moving with confidence.
      </p>
      <h3>Exercises to Explore</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Chair sit-to-stands.</li>
        <li>Farmer carries with light weights.</li>
        <li>Supported step-ups.</li>
        <li>Standing resistance-band exercises.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>



  <section class="strength-equipment">
    <p class="eyebrow">Recommended Equipment</p>
    <p>
      Having the right equipment can make strength training
      more convenient and enjoyable. Explore this Olympic
      weightlifting barbell set for your home workout space.
    </p>

    <div class="strength-product">
      <h3>Olympic Weightlifting Barbell Set</h3>
      <p>
        Build strength and support your home workout routine
        with this Olympic-style weightlifting barbell set.
        A practical addition to a home gym for resistance
        training, weightlifting, and strength development.
      </p>

      <a
        class="strength-product-button"
        href="https://www.amazon.ca/Yaheetech-Olympic-Lifting-Exercise-Barbell/dp/B07CZLBDYF?crid=11P3WS0BUHEWZ&dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.Wgcp9SQPQUkwpzP5-CYFGHf347ea_vN94_D_pT1-N7dfAIRrZ_CdIpBLaccVYelduBytcCw8Qyj0ENLAGf78pWNxiIUUG49d3N4BdeM9kcSDM0Fo-1qDdKdhwFONXaTYrH_v-LQn4qfDYSH4R0DxxxG1TFN4fVThV7aV9beB3y6-OpSY91zb_82LXC6kJktNjq7AlQUL14m5oRT1le-ZHjISYZge6B2-cO0hUZg3WZwnHQkFzb8RnmunHnOXgdrfcqY2wMaxN_pN8Fgbgw-p7GrE57APzwCQnqMsw5929Ro.xK5YTwY0EAI4ct48iNiUV8AnzRpvW8uUDepw2V5AW2Q&dib_tag=se&keywords=weight%2Bset&qid=1795631659&sprefix=weight%2Bset%2Bst%2Caps%2C399&sr=8-24&th=1&gaOptInStatus=true&linkCode=ll2&tag=silkenvalleyl-20&linkId=1674d0bf9ad82f62b4d5e191dacb225e&gaOptInStatus=true&ref_=as_li_ss_tl"
        target="_blank"
        rel="sponsored nofollow noopener"
      >
        Weightlifting Equipment
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="strength-routine">
    <p class="eyebrow">Consistency</p>
    <h2>Creating a Weekly Strength Routine</h2>
    <p>
      A balanced weekly routine allows different muscle groups
      to work while providing time for recovery. Here is an
      example of a simple schedule that can be adjusted to
      individual experience and fitness levels.
    </p>

    <div class="strength-table">
      <div class="strength-row">
        <strong>Monday</strong>
        <span>Upper-body strength exercises</span>
      </div>
      <div class="strength-row">
        <strong>Tuesday</strong>
        <span>Walking or gentle cardio</span>
      </div>
      <div class="strength-row">
        <strong>Wednesday</strong>
        <span>Lower-body strength exercises</span>
      </div>
      <div class="strength-row">
        <strong>Thursday</strong>
        <span>Rest, stretching, or gentle movement</span>
      </div>
      <div class="strength-row">
        <strong>Friday</strong>
        <span>Full-body strength exercises</span>
      </div>
      <div class="strength-row">
        <strong>Saturday</strong>
        <span>Walking or recreational activity</span>
      </div>
      <div class="strength-row">
        <strong>Sunday</strong>
        <span>Rest and recovery</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="strength-note">
    <h2>Build Strength Gradually</h2>
    <p>
      Start with light resistance and a manageable number
      of repetitions. Prioritize good technique over heavier
      weights, and increase resistance gradually as exercises
      become more comfortable. Allow adequate recovery between
      sessions and stop if an exercise causes pain.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="strength-links">
    <h2>Explore More Workouts</h2>
    <div class="strength-link-grid">
      <a href="/fitness/workouts/cardio/">Cardio Workouts →</a>
      <a href="/fitness/workouts/home/">Home Workouts →</a>
      <a href="/fitness/workouts/low-impact/">Low-Impact Exercise →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="strength-back">
    <a href="/fitness/workouts/">← Return to Workouts</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .strength-intro {
    margin: 30px 0;
    padding: 28px;
    background: var(--rose-wash);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .strength-intro h2,
  .strength-routine h2,
  .strength-note h2,
  .strength-links h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .strength-intro p,
  .strength-routine > p:not(.eyebrow),
  .strength-note p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .strength-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 35px 0;
  }

  .strength-card {
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .strength-number {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .strength-card h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0 0 13px;
  }

  .strength-card h3 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    margin: 22px 0 10px;
  }

  .strength-card p,
  .strength-card li {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .strength-card p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .strength-card ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .strength-routine {
    margin: 40px 0;
  }

  .strength-routine .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .strength-table {
    margin-top: 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .strength-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 130px 1fr;
    gap: 15px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .strength-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .strength-row strong {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
  }

  .strength-row span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .strength-note {
    padding: 30px;
    margin: 40px 0;
    background: var(--rose-wash);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .strength-links {
    margin: 40px 0;
  }

  .strength-link-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 15px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .strength-link-grid a {
    display: block;
    padding: 18px;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background 0.2s ease;
  }

  .strength-link-grid a:hover {
    background: var(--rose-wash);
  }

  .strength-back {
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .strength-back a {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .strength-back a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .strength-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .strength-link-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .strength-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 5px;
    }
  }
</style>

